msgid "The number after ``sensorValue`` is the **raw** reading of the probe. Ignore the percentage for now - it is not calibrated yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:220
msgid "Calibrate the probe, because every probe and every soil is different:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:222
msgid "Hold the probe **in the air** (dry) and write down the ``sensorValue``, for example ``535``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:224
msgid "Put the probe **in a glass of water** and write down the second ``sensorValue``, for example ``280``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:226
msgid "Put both numbers into the sketch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:233
msgid "Upload again. Now the percentage really means something: 0 % is as dry as the air, 100 % is as wet as the water."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:238
msgid "The probe reads **higher when dry and lower when wet** - that is why the two numbers appear in this order in the formula. If you skip the calibration the percentage is still shown, but the gauge may sit at 0 % in damp soil or at 100 % in dry soil."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:247
msgid "On the dashboard, drag the **slider** to a value above the current moisture (for example 40) and turn **Auto Mode** on. Within 35 seconds the pump starts, and the gauge begins to climb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:253
msgid "The pump only ever runs when **Auto Mode** is on. With the switch off you can watch the readings for as long as you like and the pump stays quiet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:261
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:263
msgid "**Blynk account and libraries**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:265
msgid "The first three lines say which Blynk device this board belongs to. They come from the device page and are identical in every project of this kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:276
msgid "**The serial port that talks to the module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:278
msgid "The ESPC2-01 works as a modem: the sketch sends it AT commands on D0/D1, which is ``Serial1``, a hardware port. ``espModuleInit()`` waits for the module to boot and then sends ``ATE0`` so the replies stop carrying a copy of the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:288
msgid "**The pump**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:296
msgid "The pump runs through an **L9110** driver. Give ``1A`` a HIGH level and the pump turns; ``1B`` stays LOW, it is only needed to reverse a motor. A relay or a simple transistor would work the same way - one pin, on or off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:300
msgid "**The probe and its two calibration points**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:308
msgid "The probe returns a raw number, and - this is the surprising part - **the wetter the soil, the lower the number**. The sketch turns that into a percentage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:315
msgid "With the two calibration values this maps \"in water\" to ``1.0`` and \"in air\" to ``0.0``, and everything in between proportionally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:318
msgid "**Two timers, two different jobs**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:325
msgid "Measuring is cheap, so it happens often. Starting a pump is not, so it is checked more slowly - and ``delay()`` is never used, so the Blynk connection keeps running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:328
msgid "**BLYNK_CONNECTED() and the two writes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:340
msgid "``BLYNK_CONNECTED()`` runs at every connection, including after a power cut, and asks the server for the slider and the switch. Without it a restarted board would water with a threshold of ``0`` - that is, never."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:344
msgid "**sendData() - report, autoWater() - act**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:360
msgid "``sendData()`` only reads and reports - it never touches the pump. ``autoWater()`` is the only place that starts it, and it needs **both** conditions: the automatic mode on, and the soil drier than your slider."
msgstr ""
